course: dictionary
lesson: 888
title: Bird
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bird is an animal with feathers, wings and a beak. Birds lay eggs, and most birds can fly. Look for these clues when you meet the word in a text.
explain: Bird is a noun, and the plural is birds. You can count birds: one bird, two birds, a flock of birds. You can say birds come, or birds fly away.
explain: «Darwin's finches have beaks suited to seeds, insects or cactus.» Here the word bird is used in science, to mean a group of animals with feathers. Context tells you which sense is meant.
fact: A bird is an animal with feathers, wings and a beak.
fact: Birds lay eggs, and most birds can fly.
fact: «Early bird» and «birds of a feather» are phrases that use the word bird, but they do not mean a real bird.
fact: «Birds may nest in a nest box in spring.» A bird's nest is where birds lay their eggs.
fact: In science, birds are a group of animals, and the group is named after the same word.
exercise: «Darwin's finches have beaks suited to seeds, insects or cactus.» Which part of a bird is this sentence about? | Its nest | Its eggs | *Its beak | Its tail
exercise: Which of these is a bird? | A bat | *A robin | A frog | A whale
exercise: What is a bird? | A type of cloud | *An animal with feathers, wings and a beak | A plant | A kind of fish
test: Which is something most birds can do? | Dig tunnels underground | Climb up and down trees like a monkey | Swim deep under the sea | *Fly
test: Which phrase uses the word bird? | Break a leg | *Birds of a feather | Cold feet | Once in a blue moon
exam: Which is true about birds? | Birds never lay eggs | Birds have fins instead of wings | *Most birds can fly | Birds have no beaks
